---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {roots,qualities} from '../../lib/coreCatalog.js';
import {coreChordByKey,coreChordKeyboard} from '../../lib/chordAtlas.mjs';
import {prettyNote} from '../../lib/music.js';
import PianoKeyboard from '../../components/PianoKeyboard.astro';
const starter=coreChordKeyboard(coreChordByKey.get('C:major'));
---
<BaseLayout title="Piano Chord Inversion Explorer | All 120 Chords & Slash Bass Notes" description="Explore root position and piano inversions for 120 chords across ten families. Hear each voicing, view correctly spelled notes and identify slash-chord bass notes." canonicalPath="/tools/inversion-explorer/" crumbs={[{name:'Inversion Explorer',href:'/tools/inversion-explorer/'}]}>
  <div class="container page-hero tool-hero"><span class="eyebrow">120 CHORDS · 10 FAMILIES</span><h1>Move the bass.<br/>Keep the harmony.</h1><p class="lead">From major and minor triads to suspended and half-diminished sevenths: every chord in our 120-chord atlas has a root position and all of its inversions. Select a chord to see its lowest note and hear each voicing.</p></div>
  <section class="container section-compact"><div class="two-col">
    <div class="panel tool-panel"><label for="inversion-chord" class="input-label">Choose one of 120 chords</label><select class="field" id="inversion-chord">
      {roots.map(root=><optgroup label={prettyNote(root)+' chords'}>{qualities.map(q=>{
        const c=coreChordByKey.get(root+':'+q.id);
        return <option value={root+':'+q.id} selected={root==='C'&&q.id==='major'}>{c.symbol} · {q.name}</option>;
      })}</optgroup>)}
    </select>
    <div id="inversion-tool" style="margin-top:20px" aria-live="polite">
      <h2>{starter.name}</h2><p>Original notes: <strong>{starter.notes.map(prettyNote).join(' · ')}</strong></p>
      <PianoKeyboard chord={starter}/><div class="button-row"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-play-midi={starter.inversions[0].midi.join(',')}>▶ Play root position</button></div>
    </div></div>
    <aside class="panel tool-panel"><h2>What changes?</h2><p>Root position starts on the root. First inversion places the second chord tone in the bass, second inversion the third, and a four-note chord also has a third inversion.</p><div class="note-explainer"><h3>Read slash chords</h3><p>Bm/D still means B minor, with D as the lowest chord tone. For a suspended chord, “first inversion” means the second note in that chord's stack is now the lowest, not necessarily a major or minor third.</p></div><p class="help-text">The displayed keyboard gives one reference octave, not a mandatory fingering. Move the voicing to a comfortable register as needed.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/chord-library/">Browse the 120-chord atlas ↗</a></p></aside>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
